From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/esp32: add key-bound CCMP to external ESP-NOW peer

Extend the opt-in external ESP-NOW bridge with AES-CCMP protected
management action frames. The bridge unwraps the fixture LMK using
AES-128-ECB under the configured PMK, strips the guest hardware
envelope on TX, encrypts the action body with a fresh PN and eight-byte
MIC, and authenticates RX before injecting it through the normal DMA
path. Authentication failure is dropped before guest delivery.

The PMK and wrapped LMK remain controller-local. The plaintext LMK is
not retained in device state, and PMK/LMK runtime environment values
are redacted from persisted/API session snapshots. This fixture
exercises key-bound CCMP and wrong-LMK rejection, not guest key-state
programming, replay windows, loss/retry, RF, timing or physical
hardware behavior.

Signed-off-by: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
---
 3 files changed, 315 insertions(+)

